Well, one mystery just got solved at least.

I've been waiting for this shoe to drop for several
bones file contributions from me to Hearse, now.

This is what Hearse does when it has run out of
compatible bones files to give you because you've
foolishly tried to collect one of each type and it
doesn't have all of them.

         C:\NETHAC~1\BONES>hearse Hearse ver 1.0.6d

         bonD0.5... uploaded Downloading... INFO: The
         server currently has no more bones files of
         the right version to offer you - it has kept
         track of how many files you are owed for the
         future

         This version (3.4.3 Windows) and compatible
         versions have a total of 11976 bones files.
         You uploaded 71 of them.  More stats are
         available at http://hearse.krollmark.com

         Please press any key to continue...

That's a bit of dressy software engineering. Thanks,
to someone.

